LORAN — third-party data terms
==============================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the SOFTWARE in this repository. It grants you
no rights whatsoever to the DATA the software fetches at runtime. That data is
governed by each upstream provider's own terms, and several of them are more
restrictive than MIT.

Read this before deploying this software anywhere public or commercial.

Aircraft position feeds
-----------------------
  airplanes.live   NON-COMMERCIAL use only. 1 request/second, no SLA.
  adsb.fi          Non-commercial.
  adsb.lol         ODbL 1.0 — share-alike. Redistributing a derived database
                   carries obligations; displaying positions in a browser is
                   ordinary use, but read the licence before you export.

Airframe and route detail
-------------------------
  adsbdb           Open, no published rate limit. This project sets its own
                   politeness budget rather than assuming there is none.

Photographs
-----------
  planespotters.net
                   Photo API Terms of Use apply. Notably:
                     * image binaries must NOT be downloaded, stored or
                       re-hosted — this software never touches them, the
                       browser loads them from the provider's CDN;
                     * returned URLs must not be rewritten;
                     * photographer attribution must be displayed;
                     * clause 8 forbids re-exposing their API through your own
                       API, feed, bulk export or dataset.

                   That last clause is why this project's photo endpoint is
                   owner-only by default when access tokens are configured.

Basemaps and geography
----------------------
  GEBCO            Attribution required (bathymetry and the depth readout).
  Esri             Attribution required, where used.
  NOAA / NWS NEXRAD, served via Iowa State University's Mesonet
                   US Government public domain; please credit IEM for hosting.
  OurAirports      Public domain.
  Natural Earth    Public domain.

A note on scope
---------------
This software is single-user and unauthenticated BY DESIGN, and that design is
part of what keeps it inside the non-commercial terms above. A fork that adds
multi-user hosting, a public API, or commercial use is not automatically covered
by those upstream terms, and should re-check each one.

The full terms review, with measured response shapes and verdicts, is in
docs/data-sources.md.
